 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Preprocessing is $O(N \cdot B^3)$ for $N$ bricks, with tensor decomposition overhead. Runtime complexity depends on the number of cache hits. Reconstruction on cache miss is $O(B^3 \cdot R^3)$ or similar, depending on the reconstruction method. Ray-casting is $O(\text{ray length} \cdot \text{samples})$.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Significantly reduced compared to raw data due to Tucker decomposition and quantization. The octree structure adds overhead. The GPU cache size is limited by available VRAM [S1].
-*   **Performance:** Enables interactive visualization of large datasets [S1]. Performance scales with the number of cache hits. Higher $K$ values increase reconstruction time and detail [S1].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Preprocessing is $O(N \cdot B^3)$ for $N$ bricks, with tensor decomposition overhead [S1]. Runtime complexity depends on the number of cache hits [S1]. Reconstruction on cache miss is $O(B^3 \cdot R^3)$ or similar, depending on the reconstruction method [S1]. Ray-casting is $O(\text{ray length} \cdot \text{samples})$ [S1].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Significantly reduced compared to raw data due to Tucker decomposition and quantization [S1]. The octree structure adds overhead [S1]. The adaptive loader maintains a working set on CPU and GPU memory, asynchronously fetching from the out-of-core structure [S1].
+*   **Performance:** Enables interactive visualization of large datasets [S1]. Performance scales with the number of cache hits [S1]. Higher $K$ values increase reconstruction time and detail [S1].
 *   **Strengths:** Low memory footprint, adaptive loading, interactive rank control [S1].
 *   **Limitations:** Reconstruction latency on cache misses, quantization artifacts [S1].
 
 ## Background
-The method was introduced in the paper "Interactive Multiscale Tensor Reconstruction for Multiresolution Volume Visualization" [S1]. It builds on the MOVR approach for adaptive refinement [S1, S12, S14]. It is used for interactive visualization of large volumetric datasets [S1].
